<title>USA: CBOT files to trade options on eurodollar futures.</title>
<headline>CBOT files to trade options on eurodollar futures.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board of Trade filed a proposal to trade options on eurodollar futures, according to the Federal Register.</p>
<p>In an application to the Commodity Futures Trading Commission, the CBOT asked to become a designated contract market for such options.</p>
<p>The CFTC said it would accept public comments on the proposal until October 30.</p>
<p>The CBOT originally received regulatory approval to trade eurodollar futures in 1981. The Chicago Mercantile Exchange already trades Eurodollar futures and options on those futures.</p>
</text>
